Work in progress

Automation framework using Page Object Model (POM) and Gherkin syntax with Pytest-BDD

Steps to run:
py -3.14 -m venv venv
.\venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
pip install -r requirements.txt
playwright install                      # one-time browser download for web tests
pytest -s -v --platform android         # mobile (Android)
pytest -s -v --platform ios             # mobile (iOS)
pytest -s -v --platform web             # web (Playwright)

The --platform flag (default: android) decides which suite runs. Tests under
tests/mobile/ are deselected when --platform=web, and tests/web/ are
deselected when --platform=android|ios — so a single pytest invocation
always runs exactly one target.

Mobile (Appium):
  Need Appium server and a device emulator.
  Capabilities live in config/capabilities.yaml; page objects per platform live
  under pages/mobile/<platform>/. To add iOS, implement pages/mobile/ios/*.py
  and register the classes in pages/mobile/pages.py under PAGE_CLASSES["iOS"].

Web (Playwright):
  Page objects live under pages/web/. The web_pages fixture loads WEB_BASE_URL
  (defaults to https://www.saucedemo.com/) before each test.
  Web and mobile share the same .feature files under tests/features/.